          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is RHYTHM FUN a good treadmill brand?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It is a budget brand with its own US store and real prices. Its 13% incline walking pad with handlebars has speed, capacity and belt figures that an independent listing summary confirms; the rest of the current range rests on RHYTHM FUN’s figures alone, and the warranty is one year.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the best RHYTHM FUN walking pad?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On 5 November 2026, the RHYTHM FUN 13% Incline Walking Pad with Handle Bar at $209.99: 0.6 to 6.2 mph, a 300 lb capacity, a 37.5 by 15-inch belt, a 3.9-inch folded height and three manual incline positions to 13%, with side handlebars.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Are the RHYTHM FUN AP01 and AP02 discontinued?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              They appear to be. A walking-pad tracker recorded both as removed from Amazon US by February 2026, and neither was in RHYTHM FUN’s store catalogue on 5 November 2026. Any you find for sale are likely old stock or second-hand.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the RHYTHM FUN incline treadmill have a motorised incline?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. Every RHYTHM FUN treadmill and walking pad on its store on 5 November 2026 used a manual incline, set by hand at two or three fixed positions with the belt stopped, from 8% on the S8 to 13% on the current walking pads.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Has there been a RHYTHM FUN treadmill recall?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              We searched the CPSC recall database for RHYTHM FUN by title and manufacturer on 5 November 2026 and found no recall. Check your model number on the CPSC site, since marketplace products are sometimes recorded under another company’s name.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is RHYTHM FUN the same as YPOO?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              They appear to be linked. RHYTHM FUN’s pads use the YPOOFIT app, and its S8 treadmill’s description calls it a “YPOO treadmill”. We could not confirm that individual models are identical, but it is worth comparing a RHYTHM FUN with any YPOO pad that shares its photos and figures.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

